Id: required-check-runs-on-every-change
Pattern: paths-ignore
Subject: .github/workflows/build.yaml .github/workflows/test.yaml
Except: none
Issue: 154

These two workflows produce `call / build` and `call / test`, which the branch
ruleset on the default branch requires. A required context is satisfied by a run
that reports success and by nothing else, so a workflow that declines to start
does not skip a check, it withholds one, and the merge is refused for a context
that is missing.

Both files carried a trigger path filter ignoring Markdown. The effect was not
that documentation changes skipped a build. It was that documentation changes
could not be merged at all, and three pull requests sat in that state before
anybody read the block as one defect rather than as three.

The rule is written against the trigger key rather than against the glob,
because the glob is not the mistake. Any path filter on either of these two
workflows removes a class of change from what the gate can speak about, and
which class it is only decides who notices.

Its bound is the file list above. A third workflow added later to produce a
required context is not covered here, because this rule cannot read the required
set: that set is a repository setting and no part of it is in the tree. Whoever
raises the required set widens `Subject`, and #40 is where that set is chosen.
